#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""chiron-rice: the Chiron Stick desktop theme ("Clinic Night"). The whole desktop takes its colours
from the current wallpaper: wallust extracts a palette, this script checks contrast and turns it into
GTK, panel, terminal, rofi, btop, conky, starship, fastfetch and folder-icon colours. Runs as the
desktop user. Verdict colours in chiron's reports never come from here (CLAUDE.md decision 10).
The picker and the animated wallpaper changes are in chiron-walls.

  chiron-rice apply <image>        set the wallpaper (animated) and re-theme everything from it
  chiron-rice pick                 choose a wallpaper: full-screen picker with a live theme preview
  chiron-rice random               random wallpaper from the current set
  chiron-rice next                 timer tick: random wallpaper (personal mode, not paused)
  chiron-rice mode client|personal calm wallpapers on other people's PCs / the full collection
  chiron-rice pause | resume       stop / restore rotation and the compositor (chiron stress does this)
  chiron-rice animations on|off    animated wallpaper changes (on by default)
  chiron-rice login                session start: end a leftover pause, compositor on or off, start conky
  chiron-rice status
  chiron-rice thumbs               build the wallpaper thumbnail cache
  chiron-rice install-user         one-time desktop setup for this user (panels, keys, fonts, autostart)
"""
